# Local working material — PR dumps, issue exports, one-off notes. Kept next
# to the project so it is not scattered across the filesystem, but never
# committed: large, regenerable from `gh`, and stale within a day.
.local-archive/
test_output.txt

# project-intelligence skill output. Regenerated from the code on demand:
#   python3 ~/Desktop/Projects/project-intelligence/scripts/analyze-project.py \
#       --project-dir . --output-dir .project-intelligence
#
# Deliberately NOT committed, and deliberately NOT written into docs/.
# docs/database-schema.md is hand-maintained and enforced by
# backend/scripts/spec_check.py and check_migration_integrity.py — it is the
# source of truth for the schema. A generated docs/database.md sitting beside it
# would be a second, weaker answer to the same question, and whichever one a
# reader happened to open would look authoritative. Committing generated docs
# also guarantees they go stale between regenerations, which is the exact drift
# this project has spent real time unpicking.
.project-intelligence/
graphify-out/
AGENTS.md

# Generated database backups
/backups/